%description:
Test connection setup with a forking listener (B): an RST in SYN_RCVD closes
the forked connection. A sends its SYN and closes at once, so its TCP answers
B's SYN-ACK with an RST. The forked connection closes, and B keeps one
connection, its listener. The app does not know the forked connection (no
ACCEPT yet), so it gets no indication. Before, the forked connection returned
to LISTEN, and B had two listeners.

%inifile: omnetpp.ini
[General]
record-vector-results = false
ned-path = .;../../../../src;../../lib

cmdenv-express-mode=false

*.testing=true
cmdenv-log-prefix="[%c]: "

*.srv_app.fork=true
*.cli_app.tClose=0.0015s

include ../../lib/defaults.ini

%#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
%postrun-command: grep "^\[testing\]\|finishing with" test.out > test_1.out || true
%contains: test_1.out
[testing]: srv_tcp: SYN_RCVD --> CLOSED  (on RCV_RST)
[]: TcpTestNet1.cli_tcp: finishing with 0 connections open.
[]: TcpTestNet1.srv_tcp: finishing with 1 connections open.
%#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
%postrun-command: grep "undisposed object:" test.out > test_undisposed.out || true
%not-contains: test_undisposed.out
undisposed object: (
%#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
